<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuelan M-2 falls 0.38 pct in week to Oct 25.</title>
<headline>Venezuelan M-2 falls 0.38 pct in week to Oct 25.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuelan money supply, as measured by the monetary aggregate M-2, fell 0.38 percent or 17 billion bolivars to 4.391 trillion bolivars in the week to October 25, the central bank said.</p>
<p>At the beginning of 1996, M-2 was 3.530 trillion bolivars.</p>
<p>-- Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600</p>
</text>
